Goodix GM168 Linux driver provenance
====================================

This repository contains an experimental libfprint driver and integration
overlay for USB device 27c6:589a. The implementation is licensed under
LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Upstream base
-------------
libfprint v1.94.100, commit 80a4b5ec612892c5c056c48dddaa561452cf37ec
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libfprint/libfprint

Driver lineage
--------------
The driver sources in driver/ build on:
https://github.com/mrcook1e-ai/goodix-gm168
starting from commit 7f7e3710bd6405b6bc238cf85fecb74e61b4d0da
and subsequent hardening/overlay collaboration with:
Daniil Yakoshinov (libfprint-goodix-gm168).

The original repository supplied the initial GM168 USB protocol, TLS-PSK
transport, asynchronous libfprint state machines, image-processing pipeline, and
build integration. Credit belongs to repository maintainer mrcook1e-ai (Oleg),
contributor wseng, and the AI co-authorship disclosed in the repository commit
history.

Subsequent 27c6:589a hardware validation, security/lifecycle hardening, and
clean overlay restructuring were performed by Daniil Yakoshinov in 2026, followed
by SIGFM matching integration, GFUSB firmware/capture updates, and OpenSSL 3
dependency selection.

Parts of the Goodix transport/TLS implementation derive from the
55b4-experimental libfprint work by Alexander Meiler, Matthieu Charette,
and Alireza S.N., also licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later.

SIGFM matching integration
--------------------------
The SIGFM (Scale-Invariant Geometric Feature Matching) subsystem included in
patches/libfprint-v1.94.100-integration.patch derives from the SIGFM
implementation by:
- Matthieu Charette <matthieu.charette@gmail.com>
- Natasha England-Elbro <ashenglandelbro@protonmail.com>
- Timur Mangliev <tigrmango@gmail.com>
licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later, adapted for libfprint v1.94.100 and small
capacitive sensors with enrollment anti-duplication and verify retry support.

The reciprocal matching, tiled capture-coverage gate, deferred-deactivation
lifecycle, and experimental post-RANSAC translation-consensus A/B variant were
adapted from the Goodix 27c6:581a implementation by Space-Dev0:
https://github.com/Space-Dev0/goodix-fingerprint-drivers
also licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later. The GM168 integration retains its own
SIFT parameters, Lowe ratio, RANSAC model, scale/inlier bounds, SGFM v1 format,
and production defaults; translation consensus is not enabled by the driver.

Clean-room provenance note
--------------------------
The 27c6:589a protocol and image-processing path were studied from USB traffic
and behavior of the lawfully installed Windows driver. No Goodix or Microsoft
executable, firmware, VM image, private key, per-device calibration file,
biometric sample, or packet capture is distributed here.
